@@ -6,6 +6,50 @@ The DS Bot plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek
 
 Tested with dsh `0.2.1-alpha.1` (Web and Desktop) on Linux.
 
+## Kelivo sync (test build)
+
+This checkout adds chat-history sync with the Kelivo Sync M1 server. The sync bridge
+has been tested with DSH `0.2.0-rc.2`, DS Bot `0.1.3`, and Kelivo `1.3.1`.
+**Bot settings → Kelivo sync** pairs this desktop with the server using a one-use
+pairing code. Pair Kelivo with a separate code on the same server.
+
+**Share a Bot chat** creates a Kelivo conversation containing that Bot's own-chat
+history, including earlier conversation parts. **Import a phone chat** creates a
+new Bot with that history; select its model before sending your next message.
+The bridge copies both user and assistant messages into the canonical DSH Session,
+so subsequent model requests include them. It never sends queued prompts, wakes a
+Bot, calls a model, or invokes tools. Automatic sync runs every minute while DSH
+is running; **Sync now** runs it immediately. Model routes, keys, system prompts,
+Bot permissions, group chats, memory, and attachment files remain device-local.
+
+Phone edits update the model-visible message through DSH's public projection API;
+the original audit log remains intact. Deleting a phone conversation pauses that
+link and retains the desktop Bot. Deleting a desktop Bot deletes its linked phone
+conversation. Edits to compacted/archived history append an explicit correction
+to the active context rather than rewriting an old checkpoint. Keep the sync
+plugin installed to replay edited histories. The server stores text in plaintext;
+use HTTPS outside explicit localhost/private-network testing.
+
+Test installation must use a separate `DSH_HOME` and test profile. Do not replace
+the user's existing plugin or point the test bench at their live data. On Windows,
+the existing custom DS Bot client and session-header patches must be preserved
+when installing into the production profile after testing.
+
+The keyless cross-client check uses the real DSH mock bench and real Go server,
+then captures the actual Kelivo model request:
+
+```sh
+npm ci && npm run harness && npm run build
+DSH_HARNESS="$PWD/dev/harness" CONTEXT_WINDOW=100000 CHECK_RATIO=0.45 \
+  dev/bench.sh kelivo-sync 3098 8798 start
+KELIVO_SYNC_SERVER_BINARY=/path/to/kelivo-sync FLUTTER_BIN=/path/to/flutter \
+  KELIVO_REPO=/path/to/kelivo node dev/kelivo-sync-smoke.mjs kelivo-sync 3098
+DSH_HARNESS="$PWD/dev/harness" dev/bench.sh kelivo-sync 3098 8798 stop
+```
+
+`npm test` checks retry receipts, restart replay, role preservation and no Bot
+wakeups against the Go server when `KELIVO_SYNC_SERVER_BINARY` is set.
+
 ## Features
 
 - **Long-lived Bots**: each Bot is a dsh Session in the "DS Bot" workspace, with its own name, role, instructions and model.
